{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome that occurs with 100% probability) in each lottery. In Lottery A, the possible outcomes are 4000 Euros with 20% probability and 0 Euros with 80% probability. In Lottery B, the outcomes are 3000 Euros with 25% probability and 0 Euros with 75% probability. Neither lottery contains a sure outcome, as both involve risk and no outcome occurs with 100% probability. Therefore, the condition for applying the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome) is not met in either lottery. The reason would be indifferent or unable to make a choice since neither lottery has a sure outcome.",
